march is nutrition month and you don't  have to overhaul your diet completely  to eat healthier and feel your best  registered dietitian  mia sin shares three simple nutrition  tips that anyone can follow plus some  delicious recipes  that you can make at home hey las vegas  now it's national nutrition month and  you don't have to overhaul your diet  completely  to eat healthier and feel your best  today i have three simple nutrition tips  plus some recipes that you can make at  home my first tip is to snack smarter  wonderful pistachios are what i call a  snack with staying power because one  serving provides six grams of  plant-based protein  and three grams of filling fiber plus  nearly ninety percent of the fats found  in pistachios are the better for you  mono and polyunsaturated type so you get  a protein fiber fat trio that may help  keep you fuller longer pair with a piece  of fruit or whole grain crackers to  build a balanced snack  my next nutrition tip is to rethink your  beverages  replace sugar sweetened beverages with  nutrient-dense options like florida  orange juice which contributes vitamins  minerals and antioxidants including  folate potassium and vitamin c  a common misconception about orange  juice is that it's jam-packed with added  sugars  in truth 100 orange juice doesn't  contain any added sugar  the sweetness you taste comes from the  naturally occurring sugars that develop  as oranges grow  making it a nutritious replacement for  sugar sweetened beverages  add it to baked goods smoothies or  homemade salad dressings for a boost of  nutrition  and to help reach your daily fruit  intake recommendation  smoothies are another nutritious  beverage option and an easy way to help  you meet your recommended five servings  of fruits and veggies for the day  to a blender add frozen mango and  pineapple a half cup of greek yogurt  one cup of 100 orange juice and one  teaspoon of icelandic wild fish oil  which adds omega-3 fats important for  brain and heart health plus  ostaxanthin a powerful antioxidant found  in seafood  important for brain eye skin and immune  health if you aren't a seafood fan this  is a good alternative that allows you to  reap the benefits of omega-3 fats in a  clean tasting liquefied form that you  can add to smoothies or recipes  you can find it on amazon my last  nutrition tip is to satisfy sweet  cravings with desserts with benefits  try these melt in your mouth sweet  potato collagen brownies add one cooked  sweet potato to a food processor with a  third cup of nut butter  three tablespoons of maple syrup a  fourth cup of cacao powder and one scoop  of sparkle wellness skin boost plus  varisol collagen powder which comes in  unflavored and flavored varieties like  orange and tropical  some research suggests that taking  collagen daily may help  improve skin appearance and elasticity  while minimizing unwanted signs of aging  bake in a lined bread pan for 20 minutes  at 350 degrees fahrenheit  i hope you enjoyed these recipes and  tips you can find them at my website  nutritionbymia  and nutritionbymia on instagram where i  also share meal ideas and nutrition tips  daily  desserts with benefits okay we always  love your tips thank you mia
 

